            final ctx = rootNavigatorKey.currentContext;
            if (ctx != null && ctx.mounted) {
              ctx.go(AuthRoutePaths.login);
            }
          },
```

```274:278:apps/glasses_app/lib/app.dart
        onUnsupportedDeviceTypeProvider.overrideWithValue((item) {
          final ctx = rootNavigatorKey.currentContext;
          if (ctx != null && ctx.mounted) {
            AppToast.info(ctx, GlassesShellL10n.of(ctx).comingSoon);
          }
```

A third usage is in `deviceRoutes()` — the search→connect bridge pushes via `navigatorKey.currentContext` (same key passed in):

```48:51:packages/widget/device/widget_device/lib/src/routing/device_routes.dart
              final ctx = navigatorKey.currentContext;
              if (ctx != null && ctx.mounted) {
                ctx.push(DeviceRoutePaths.connect, extra: device);
              }
```

**Tests navigate directly on the global router:**

```34:34:apps/glasses_app/test/widget_test.dart
    appRouter.go('${ProfileRoutePaths.settings}?token=secret-token');
```

**No notification-tap → route wiring.** `core_notification` exposes schedule/cancel only; `FlutterLocalNotificationService.initialize()` has no `onDidReceiveNotificationResponse` / tap handler. Notifications are initialized in `main.dart` but only for scheduling (device schedule reminders).

**Shared pattern:** `apps/pkg_showcase/lib/src/app_router.dart` mirrors this with `rootNavKey` + `appRouter`.

**Routing abstraction:** `packages/core/core_base/lib/src/routing/router_registry.dart` defines `RouteGroup` — features export route groups; the App aggregates them.

---

### 2. Deep-link packages (`app_links`, `uni_links`, etc.)

**None found anywhere in the repo.**

- Grep across all `pubspec.yaml`: no `app_links`, `uni_links`, or `flutter_deep_linking`
- Grep across `pubspec.lock`: no matches
- Grep across Dart sources: no `DeepLinkService`, `getInitialLink`, `linkStream`, etc.

`glasses_app/pubspec.yaml` uses `go_router: ^17.3.0` but no deep-link plugin.

